// A block-bodied match arm (`pattern => { stmts }`, aether F1) produces no value — blocks are
// statement sequences in Noeta, so a block-bodied function yields `unit` unless it `return`s. Using
// such an arm where the `match`'s value is consumed (here a binding RHS) would silently contribute
// `unit`, so it is a compile error (E0055) rather than a silent value loss. The fix is a value
// expression (`=> <expr>`) or moving the `match` to statement position.
// expect: error E0055 at 11:5
// expect: exit 1
x = 2
r = match x {
    1 => "one",
    2 => { t = "tw"; t ~ "o" },
    _ => "many",
}
echo "r=" ~ r
